-- dnai: promoted from tools/spec_r540.json (the THE DSG DEEPEARTH AREAS 14-15, R540: printed pp. 86-88 (pdf 87-89) - the individual area key crosses the reclaimed lakebed and the great water: Area 14 Reclaimed Caverns (the former subterranean lake almost completely filled with water, drained only by the diligent pech miners' blocked waterways - the two north inflows and south outflow continuations; the Area 5 river made dangerous by its 500-foot waterfall into a deep pool, then running placid beneath about six feet of airspace; the eastern river diving underground at the base of a mountain waterfall plunging several thousand feet through a sinkhole, rapid all the way to Area 14 but keeping a 10-foot minimum airspace and a navigable sinkhole access; the three long narrow parallel caves east-west, each opening onto the river and united by connecting passages; the heroic walls-of-stone dikes holding the water out while small streams still flow; the pech bridge over the eastern river at the middle cavern's end, joining the partially excavated 8-by-12-foot descending cavern of many miles; the water-polished uniformly smooth floors, walls and ceilings devoid of formations; the well-organized 300-miner community at the middle cavern's center with its iron and copper deposits; the monster roster - scrags, shambling mounds, a gibbering mouther, cave crickets, throat leeches, ropers, an owl bear, rust monsters and cockatrices; the Area 15 kuo-toan sabotage war - dikes damaged, rivers diverted, 20-to-25-strong war parties every few months, always defeated but never ceasing; the fanatically guarded copper and iron ore stockpiles; and the engineering marvels - the drains and centrifugal pump powered by the bridge-side giant water wheel, the lever-shifted ventilation over the coal-burning smelting plant and forge venting through a one-foot aperture to a remote mountain valley, and the stone town with its buildings stacked three or four deep and its ore wagons blocking the avenues), and Area 15 the Upper Lake of Deepearth (the almost completely water-filled chamber on its rock walls and columns, the level a dozen or more feet short of the ceiling, boat-traversable over most of its extent; the west shoreline shelf - 10 to 400 feet wide, the only dry land, reached through the partly carved dry tunnel from Area 6 with its intelligent-built stone piers and the 50% chance of 1d6 moored longboats; the cold still waters 10 to 100 feet deep, marred only where the twin Area 14 rivers enter; the center drain hole matching its outflow to the inflow, regulated by the kuo-toa and their boulder works; the great kuo-toan numbers and the blind fish of the inky depths; the domes over food-raising, quarters, hatcheries, government and recreation with their breathable air pockets where escape is virtually impossible; the giant catfish, pike, gar, lamprey, trout, perch and salmon, the water nagas, giant otters, giant crabs, giant snapping turtles, scrags and lacedons; the aboleth - perhaps the most purely evil denizens in all Deepearth, avoiding the kuo-toa but seizing all others as slaves; the aquatic fungi and brown algae with no minerals known; and the domed city by the drain - six hexagonal major domes, 150 feet across and 50 high with 20 feet of air, their corridors and rooms nested around the swim-through elevator holes));
