f Deepearth (the almost completely water-filled chamber on its rock walls and columns, the level a dozen or more feet short of the ceiling, boat-traversable over most of its extent; the west shoreline shelf - 10 to 400 feet wide, the only dry land, reached through the partly carved dry tunnel from Area 6 with its intelligent-built stone piers and the 50% chance of 1d6 moored longboats; the cold still waters 10 to 100 feet deep, marred only where the twin Area 14 rivers enter; the center drain hole matching its outflow to the inflow, regulated by the kuo-toa and their boulder works; the great kuo-toan numbers and the blind fish of the inky depths; the domes over food-raising, quarters, hatcheries, government and recreation with their breathable air pockets where escape is virtually impossible; the giant catfish, pike, gar, lamprey, trout, perch and salmon, the water nagas, giant otters, giant crabs, giant snapping turtles, scrags and lacedons; the aboleth - perhaps the most purely evil denizens in all Deepearth, avoiding the kuo-toa but seizing all others as slaves; the aquatic fungi and brown algae with no minerals known; and the domed city by the drain - six hexagonal major domes, 150 feet across and 50 high with 20 feet of air, their corridors and rooms nested around the swim-through elevator holes)",
